{"is_source_file": true, "format": "JavaScript React JSX", "description": "The file defines a React component named App that implements a simple drawing application. It includes functionalities for drawing on a canvas with different colors and brush sizes, resizing the canvas dynamically, and saving the drawing as a PNG image. The component manages state for theme, stroke color, brush size, and includes event handlers for drawing interactions using pointer events.", "external_files": ["./App.css"], "external_methods": ["document.documentElement.setAttribute", "window.devicePixelRatio", "canvas.getContext", "canvas.setPointerCapture", "canvas.getBoundingClientRect", "document.createElement", "document.body.appendChild", "a.href", "a.click", "a.remove", "window.addEventListener", "window.removeEventListener"], "published": ["clearCanvas", "saveAsImage"], "classes": [], "methods": [{"name": "App()", "description": "React functional component that renders a drawing application with canvas and control UI.", "scope": "", "scopeKind": ""}, {"name": "get2DContext", "description": "Retrieves the 2D drawing context from the canvas element."}, {"name": "setCanvasSizeToContainer", "description": "Resizes the canvas to match the container size, preserving existing drawing content, and accounts for device pixel ratio for crisp lines."}, {"name": "getPointFromEvent", "description": "Converts a pointer event to a coordinate point relative to the canvas."}, {"name": "beginStroke", "description": "Starts a new drawing stroke, captures pointer, and draws an initial dot."}, {"name": "continueStroke", "description": "Continues the drawing stroke by drawing a line from the last point to the current pointer position."}, {"name": "endStroke", "description": "Ends the current drawing stroke."}, {"name": "clearCanvas", "description": "Clears the entire canvas and sets a white background."}, {"name": "saveAsImage", "description": "Exports the current canvas drawing as a PNG image and triggers